   230	//
   231	// Install markers are fingerprinted around the same window, but a marker is
   232	// only half the evidence: an entry that is removed, replaced, corrupted, or
   233	// loses its protected provenance changes a compiled verdict without touching a
   234	// single marker byte. Planning inspects the cache while no lock is held, so
   235	// without this second look a status run could publish a stale `current` — or a
   236	// stale drift code — for state that had already moved.
