  1199	// assertProtectedCacheStateThatMovedDuringTheCheck closes the other half of the
  1200	// classification window.
  1201	//
  1202	// Install markers are fingerprinted around the whole run, but a marker is only
  1203	// half the evidence a compiled verdict is derived from: the protected cache is
  1204	// inspected once, during a read-only plan that holds no lock, and an entry that
  1205	// is removed, corrupted, or loses its provable protection afterwards changes
  1206	// every verdict taken from it without touching a single marker byte.
  1207	//
  1208	// The cache really moves here, between the plan and the classification, exactly
  1209	// as a concurrent install, sweep, or permission change would move it. Nothing
  1210	// rewrites a marker, so a verdict that stays authoritative could only have come
  1211	// from evidence nobody re-read.
